Usage: sync [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --from <FROM>                
  -t, --to <TO>                    
  -o, --only <ONLY>                Only sync these artists (semicolon-separated)
      --release <RELEASE>          Re-sync a single release by its LocalRelease ID
      --artist-hint <ARTIST_HINT>  With --release: prefer this Artist ID when the release has multiple main artists (e.g. the download's own artist, so a collab release syncs/validates under the artist it was actually downloaded for, not whichever main artist sorts first alphabetically)
      --overwrite                  
      --exact                      Exact match for --only (no prefix matching)
      --skip-artist-img            
      --skip-release-img           
      --skip-mb-tags               Skip writing MusicBrainz IDs back to audio file tags
      --only-write-mb-to-files     Write DB-known MB IDs to file tags (no API calls), then exit
      --catalogue-gaps             Fast pass: populate MISSING catalogue entries only (few API calls/artist)
      --artist-ids <ARTIST_IDS>    Read artist IDs from file (one per line, used by refresh)
      --verbose                    
      --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>  How many artists to sync at once. All workers share one MusicBrainz pacing schedule, so this changes how much of the rate allowance is used, never the rate itself [default: 6]
      --web                        Emit PROGRESS:{json} lines and plain output for the web terminal. Default is pretty colored console output
  -h, --help                       Print help
